Key Takeaways for Interviews

Direct object creation is not allowed for interfaces and abstract classes.

Polymorphism: You can reference them using their type and assign an object of a subclass (for abstract class) or implementing class (for interface).

Anonymous classes allow quick instantiation without creating a separate concrete class.